---
alwaysApply: true
---

@rule cursor_contract
INPUT: { limit: number(1..100), cursor?: string, sortBy?: keyof T, order?: 'ASC'|'DESC' }
OUTPUT: { result: T[], metaData: { nextCursor?: string, prevCursor?: string, take: number, sortBy: string, order: 'ASC'|'DESC' } }
- MUST use encodeSignedCursor/decodeSignedCursor for client-facing pagination.
- MUST NOT expose numeric offsets to clients.
- MUST support stable ordering with (sortBy, id) tuple for consistent pagination.
- SHOULD use PaginationFormatter.cursor() for consistent response format.

## Exception
Custom methods outside BaseService.listCursor() MAY use unsigned cursors (encodeCursor/decodeCursor)
for internal/specialized use cases (e.g., nested relations, custom query builders). Document these exceptions.

@example
const result = await this.listCursor({ 
  limit: q.limit, 
  cursor: q.cursor, 
  sortBy: 'createdAt', 
  order: 'DESC' 
});
return result; // Already formatted by BaseService

@example signed_cursor
// GOOD: Use signed cursors for client-facing pagination
const nextCursor = encodeSignedCursor({
  key: sortBy,
  order: direction,
  value: { [sortBy]: lastRecord[sortBy], id: lastRecord.id }
});

// ACCEPTABLE: Unsigned cursors for internal/specialized use only
// Document the exception when using this pattern
const internalCursor = encodeCursor({ key: sortBy, value: lastRecord[sortBy] });

// BAD: Unsigned cursors for general client-facing APIs
const nextCursor = encodeCursor({ key: sortBy, value: lastRecord[sortBy] }); // Don't do this